Boot screen: rebuild only the K114s kernels' images on the K114s.

Local change for this machine, not an upstream fix. omarchy-plymouth-set (behind the "boot screen
matches theme" action, omarchy-plymouth-set-by-theme) ends with `sudo omarchy-boot-rebuild`, which
on a Limine machine runs a bare `limine-mkinitcpio` and rebuilds the image of every installed
kernel. On this Mac that includes the held stock linux-aurora, whose image docs/esp-space.md keeps
off the EFI partition: on 2026-11-24 one boot screen change put its 79 MB image back, added a third
menu entry, left 43 MB free and stopped the next update at the space guard.

Where /proc/device-tree/compatible lists apple,k114s and Limine is the only boot loader Omarchy
manages (omarchy-boot-backend --managed), the rebuild names the installed linux-k114s* kernel
packages instead, one kernel at a time through omarchy-boot-rebuild (which keeps upstream's check
of limine-mkinitcpio's output). Limine's K114s pre-build hook checks for the space guard's
minimum plus the boot theme's size on the mounted EFI partition. Limine keeps its own lock
from that check through the rebuild, so a snapshot sync or another rebuild using the mutex
cannot take the space between the two. With any other backend or a missing hook, the
K114s rebuild refuses. Other machines are unchanged.

Refreshed 2026-11-27 for omarchy-dev 4.0.0.r8491. Root-run hardware setup keeps Omarchy's
no-rebuild path. The K114s guard covers the per-kernel rebuild from the desktop.

Paths are relative to /usr.

--- a/bin/omarchy-plymouth-set
+++ b/bin/omarchy-plymouth-set
@@ -397,6 +397,38 @@
   if (( EUID == 0 )); then
     # Hardware setup builds the boot image itself, after its last step.
     echo "Boot image not rebuilt: the unlock screen changes at the next omarchy-boot-rebuild"
+  elif grep -qx 'apple,k114s' < <(tr '\0' '\n' 2>/dev/null <"${K114S_DT_COMPATIBLE:-/proc/device-tree/compatible}"); then
+    # K114s local change: omarchy-boot-rebuild with no kernel named runs a bare limine-mkinitcpio, which
+    # rebuilds the image of every installed kernel, including the held stock linux-aurora, whose 79 MB
+    # image fills the EFI partition, adds a third boot menu entry and stops every later update
+    # (docs/esp-space.md). On the K114s, while Limine is the only boot loader Omarchy manages, only the
+    # linux-k114s* kernels' images are rebuilt, one kernel at a time through omarchy-boot-rebuild, each
+    # only when the mounted EFI partition has room for one image beside the old one. The room needed is
+    # the space guard's minimum plus the boot theme's size (a large custom logo grows every image).
+    # The K114s pre-build hook checks space after limine-mkinitcpio takes its own lock.
+    k114s_kernels=($({ pacman -Qqo /usr/lib/modules/*/modules.builtin 2>/dev/null || true; } | sort -u | sed -n -E '/^linux-k114s(-|$)/p'))
+    k114s_backend=$(omarchy-boot-backend --managed 2>/dev/null | paste -sd' ') || k114s_backend=
+    if [[ $k114s_backend != limine ]]; then
+      echo "Omarchy manages '${k114s_backend:-no}' boot images here, not Limine alone; the boot images were not rebuilt (this Mac's change covers Limine only)." >&2
+      exit 1
+    elif (( ${#k114s_kernels[@]} == 0 )); then
+      echo "No linux-k114s kernel is installed; the boot images were not rebuilt." >&2
+      exit 1
+    fi
+    if [[ ! -f /etc/boot/hooks/pre.d/00-k114s-boot-rebuild-guard || ! -x /etc/boot/hooks/pre.d/00-k114s-boot-rebuild-guard ]]; then
+      echo "The K114s Limine pre-build guard is missing or disabled. Reinstall the K114s Omarchy patches before rebuilding." >&2
+      exit 1
+    fi
+    k114s_theme=$(du -sb /usr/share/plymouth/themes/omarchy 2>/dev/null | cut -f1) || k114s_theme=
+    [[ $k114s_theme =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] || k114s_theme=67108864
+    k114s_need=$(( ${K114S_ESP_MIN_FREE:-88080384} + k114s_theme ))
+    for k114s_kernel in "${k114s_kernels[@]}"; do
+      if ! sudo K114S_PLYMOUTH_MIN_FREE="$k114s_need" omarchy-boot-rebuild "$k114s_kernel"; then
+        echo "Could not rebuild the $k114s_kernel boot image." >&2
+        echo "The boot screen changes at the next rebuild; once there is room: sudo omarchy-boot-rebuild ${k114s_kernels[*]}" >&2
+        exit 1
+      fi
+    done
   elif [[ $(omarchy-boot-backend) == none ]]; then
     sudo mkinitcpio -P
   else
